WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.677
This query creates one contact line.

00:00:02.677 --> 00:00:06.817
The name is trimmed and has repeated whitespace normalized.

00:00:06.817 --> 00:00:11.367
The email is trimmed, and NULLIF turns an empty string into NULL.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.422
The address is trimmed.

00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:18.507
CONCAT_WS joins the available pieces with a vertical-bar separator and skips NULL arguments.

00:00:18.507 --> 00:00:25.282
Run the query and inspect how missing values affect the output.

00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:30.322
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:34.907
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:34.907 --> 00:00:36.767
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:43.257
In a real setting such as a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates,

00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:50.827
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:50.827 --> 00:00:53.012
before discussing syntax.

00:00:53.012 --> 00:00:59.047
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
